# Copy to `.env.self-hosted`. Read by every service in compose.yaml; ignored
# by git. It holds no secrets: DATABASE_URL and POSTGRES_PASSWORD go in the
# ignored `.env` file, which Compose reads for interpolation, for example
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<a long random value>
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://smrt_start:<the same value>@database:5432/smrt_start
SMRT_RUNTIME_PROFILE=self-hosted
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=3000

# The `self-hosted` profile has no loopback owner bootstrap: people sign in
# through a real authentication provider, files go to a real asset store, and
# secrets come from a real secret store. Each setting names an installed
# module whose checkReadiness() probes that backing service. The web process
# and the workers refuse to start until all three answer.
# SMRT_AUTH_READINESS_MODULE=@your-org/auth-readiness
# SMRT_ASSETS_READINESS_MODULE=@your-org/assets-readiness
# SMRT_SECRETS_READINESS_MODULE=@your-org/secrets-readiness

SMRT_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4

# The assistant's provider key (the variable named by `ai.apiKeyEnv` in
# smrt.config.ts) belongs with the other secrets, not in this file.
